In the test, `text_value` is `"alpha beta🙂gamma alpha beta🙂gamma epsilon"` and `quote_candidates[(len(text_value) // 7) % len(quote_candidates)]` selects `"epsilon"`. Then `quote_count = text_value.count(selected_quote)` is `1`, so `quote_index = 1 + (len("epsilon") % 3) + 1 = 3`. In `Message.build_reply_arguments`, a truthy `quote` causes a call to `compute_quote_position_and_entities(quote, quote_index)`. That helper raises `ValueError` when the requested occurrence index does not exist, with the message `f"You requested the {index}-th occurrence of '{quote}', but this text appears only {length} times."` Since `"epsilon"` appears only once, the exact exception is:

## Answer
{"exception_message":"You requested the 3-th occurrence of 'epsilon', but this text appears only 1 times.","exception_type":"ValueError"}
